From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AndreaCovelli <andcov23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 17:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: re-add FT STA before pre-association PTK install

FT-over-DS can derive and install the PTK before the reassociation frame is
processed. If the previous association was just disassociated, hostapd may
retain a userspace STA entry after the kernel STA entry has already been
removed.

In that state the FT PTK install fails with:

  nl80211: kernel reports: key addition failed

and the following VLAN/WDS binding can fail with:

  NL80211_ATTR_STA_VLAN (...) failed: -2 (No such file or directory)

because both operations need a kernel STA entry. hostapd already has
ap_sta_re_add() for the closely related PMF FT path. Use the same helper
for FT STAs that are no longer marked associated before the first PTK
install.
This creates an unassociated kernel STA so mac80211 can accept the FT key
and defer hardware upload until association.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/23181#issuecomment-4857459727
Signed-off-by: AndreaCovelli <andcov23@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
@@ -1322,6 +1322,18 @@ static int hostapd_wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(v
 		return ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta);
 	}
 
+	/* FT-over-DS can reach PTK setup after the old driver STA entry was
+	 * removed, but before reassociation has added a new one. Re-add an
+	 * unassociated kernel STA so the following key/VLAN setup has a target.
+	 */
+	if (FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
+	    !(hapd->conf->mesh & MESH_ENABLED) && !(sta->added_unassoc) &&
+	    !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "FT: Re-add unassociated driver STA entry before PTK configuration");
+		return ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
